Author: Mohammad Zidane Kurnianto <mzidanek@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 10:09:13 2026 +0700

    fix(components): placeholder text was the same color as filled-in input text
    
    ::placeholder used var(--color-primary-900), identical to .input's
    own text color, making it impossible to tell at a glance whether a
    field had a real value or was just showing its placeholder.

[33mcommit 7290e369ebb1568d7bb3b82279387a7f1151aa76[m
Author: Mohammad Zidane Kurnianto <mzidanek@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 10:09:09 2026 +0700

    feat(accounts): custom password validators, required display name, keep email on error
    
    Replaces Django's CommonPasswordValidator (opaque 20k-word blocklist,
    no explainable reasoning) and NumericPasswordValidator with our own
    PasswordComplexityValidator — one transparent rule: must contain a
    letter and a digit. Also adds a required display_name field to
    signup (ACCOUNT_SIGNUP_FORM_CLASS), and fixes login/signup forms
    losing the submitted email on validation errors (passwords correctly
    stay cleared).

[33mcommit 67c261623e5d98ea109a5f75977d67d917e14217[m
Author: Mohammad Zidane Kurnianto <mzidanek@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 10:09:01 2026 +0700

    feat(accounts): add profile page with display name and profile picture
    
    Also fixes LOGIN_URL (was still pointing at the old /accounts/login/
    prefix after we moved allauth's URLs to root, breaking the redirect
    for any @login_required view).
    
    Note: settings.py also picks up AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS and
    ACCOUNT_SIGNUP_FORM_CLASS here since they landed in the same working
    session and the file can't be split across commits — those features
    are implemented in the next commit.

